<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="F_SetGoodAttStatus" Id="{e6cd67bb-2bd9-4b3d-9199-950e5913b39f}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    F_SetGoodAttStatus - forces the bits of an attenuator status word into the
    "good" state used by tests.

    PURPOSE
        Test helper for PMPS test fixtures. Starting from the attenuator status
        word supplied in xStatus, it sets the bits that describe a healthy,
        PMPS-governed attenuator, so code that judges attenuator health (for
        example F_AttenuatorOK) sees the attenuator as safe and stable.

        The bit layout is the one declared in ST_AttenuatorStatus:
            bit 0  AtTarget : attenuator has reached its requested transmission
            bit 1  Moving   : attenuator is travelling to a new transmission
            bit 2  LocalMode: attenuator ignores PMPS requests, follows a local
                              setpoint
            bit 3  PMPSMode : attenuator takes setpoints only from PMPS
            bit 4  OK       : no attenuator error, status is stable
            bit 5  Toggle   : unused
            bit 6  Include  : consider this device's status

        This helper sets bit 0 (AtTarget), bit 3 (PMPSMode) and bit 4 (OK) and
        leaves every other bit of the supplied word unchanged. Starting from a
        zeroed word the result therefore reads "at target, in PMPS mode, no
        errors", for which F_AttenuatorOK returns TRUE.

    USAGE
        For test code only, never for production logic. Use it wherever a test
        must present PMPS with a healthy attenuator, instead of hand-writing the
        status bits at each call site. There are no call sites for this helper
        in this library today; it is exported for test fixtures in dependent
        libraries.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Spell out the attenuator status bits next to the helper that
          synthesises a good value for them, so the pattern can be reviewed
          without cross-referencing ST_AttenuatorStatus.
        - Keep the definition of a "good" attenuator status word in one place,
          so a change of bit layout is made in a single function.
        - Record the current behaviour of the helper so a maintainer can reuse
          it safely (see NOTE).

    NOTE
        Behaviour documented here, deliberately not changed by this comment
        pass: xStatus is a by-value VAR_INPUT and the function result is never
        assigned, so the three bit writes only modify the local copy of the word
        and a caller currently receives 0 (the UINT default). Making the helper
        useful to a caller needs either xStatus declared as VAR_IN_OUT or an
        F_SetGoodAttStatus := xStatus assignment.

    HISTORY
        2020-11-18 / Alex Wallace
            Function created with the "Tests for the margin logic" change.
        2026-11-27 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header comment and the inline xStatus comment, including
            the attenuator status bit layout; documentation only, no behaviour
            change (audit finding #261, convention conv_321640e095c0).
*)
FUNCTION F_SetGoodAttStatus : UINT
VAR_INPUT
    xStatus : UINT; // Attenuator status word (ST_AttenuatorStatus layout): bits 0 AtTarget, 3 PMPSMode and 4 OK are set by this function, all other bits pass through unchanged
END_VAR
VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[xStatus.0 := 1;
xStatus.3 := 1;
xStatus.4 := 1;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>